{"nodes": [{"id": "claude_skills_smart_contracts_security_security_review", "label": "Security Review", "file_type": "document", "source_file": ".claude/skills/smart-contracts/security.md", "source_location": "Security", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Security review guide for Stellar smart contracts. Run the static analyzers, finish the checklists, document the threat model, and have the testing suite green before an audit."}, {"id": "claude_skills_smart_contracts_security_threat_model", "label": "Threat Model", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".claude/skills/smart-contracts/security.md", "source_location": "Threat model", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Assume the attacker controls every argument, transaction order and timing, every account that does not require a signature, contracts that mimic your interface, and the shape of state they can legally create, including entry counts and TTLs. They can extend your entries' TTLs."}, {"id": "claude_skills_smart_contracts_security_no_delegatecall", "label": "No delegatecall", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".claude/skills/smart-contracts/security.md", "source_location": "What the platform rules out", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Contracts cannot run foreign bytecode in their own context, so proxy-style hijacks do not exist."}, {"id": "claude_skills_smart_contracts_security_no_reentrancy", "label": "No Reentrancy", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".claude/skills/smart-contracts/security.md", "source_location": "What the platform rules out", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The host blocks reentrant calls, direct or indirect, on normal cross-contract paths. External calls are still failure, budget, and side-effect boundaries, so order state updates deliberately."}, {"id": "claude_skills_smart_contracts_security_host_auth_replay_protection", "label": "Host Auth Replay Protection", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/smart-contracts/security.md", "source_location": "What the platform rules out", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Nonces and expirations on authorization entries are enforced by the host, not by contract code. require_auth is opt-in, so forgetting it is the bug to hunt."}, {"id": "claude_skills_smart_contracts_security_missing_authorization", "label": "Missing Authorization", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/smart-contracts/security.md", "source_location": "1. Missing authorization", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every privileged path needs require_auth on the address that holds the policy, loaded from storage. require_auth on a caller-supplied who only proves the caller controls who."}, {"id": "claude_skills_smart_contracts_security_auth_replay_middleware", "label": "Auth Replay through Middleware", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/smart-contracts/security.md", "source_location": "2. Auth replay through middleware (missing outer `require_auth`)", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "If a user pre-signed an auth tree that includes an inner token.transfer, anyone can call a wrapper that never authorizes that user and consume the signature. Re-authorize at every layer that uses an address's authority. This is the most common real-world auth bug."}, {"id": "claude_skills_smart_contracts_security_reinitialization", "label": "Reinitialization Attacks", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/smart-contracts/security.md", "source_location": "3. Reinitialization attacks", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Only matters for a guarded initialize instead of __constructor, which cannot re-run. Without a check-and-set flag, anyone can call initialize and capture admin."}, {"id": "claude_skills_smart_contracts_security_arbitrary_contract_calls", "label": "Arbitrary Contract Calls", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/smart-contracts/security.md", "source_location": "4. Arbitrary contract calls", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A user-supplied contract address is arbitrary code. Allowlist it. A substitute can fail, trap, burn budget, emit misleading events, or call onward. It cannot re-enter you."}, {"id": "claude_skills_smart_contracts_security_integer_overflow", "label": "Integer Overflow", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/smart-contracts/security.md", "source_location": "5. Integer overflow/underflow", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "overflow-checks = true panics on overflow in the release profile, but checked math fails cleaner and survives a profile mistake. An unchecked negative i128 transfer withdraws from the destination. Use checked_* for 256-bit types (protocol 26+)."}, {"id": "claude_skills_smart_contracts_security_storage_key_collisions", "label": "Storage Key Collisions", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/smart-contracts/security.md", "source_location": "6. Storage key collisions", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Untyped keys can silently overwrite unrelated data. Always use a #[contracttype] key enum."}, {"id": "claude_skills_smart_contracts_security_check_then_act", "label": "Check-then-act Races", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/smart-contracts/security.md", "source_location": "7. Check-then-act races", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "State can change between transactions. Do the check and the write in one invocation, and take a slippage bound (min_out) from the caller. approve overwrites, so reducing a non-zero allowance can be front-run. Approve to 0 first, or use exact-amount auth."}, {"id": "claude_skills_smart_contracts_security_ttl_archival", "label": "TTL and Archival Failures", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/smart-contracts/security.md", "source_location": "8. TTL and archival failures", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A temporary entry can disappear forever, and a persistent entry can archive. Extend TTLs on hot paths. TTL is not a security control, because anyone can extend an entry with ExtendFootprintTTLOp. Store a deadline in the value and check it."}, {"id": "claude_skills_smart_contracts_security_cross_contract_returns", "label": "Untrusted Cross-Contract Returns", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/smart-contracts/security.md", "source_location": "9. Trusting cross-contract return values", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Validate data from other contracts. Allowlist oracles, sanity-check magnitudes, and enforce freshness."}, {"id": "claude_skills_smart_contracts_security_fee_griefing", "label": "Fee Griefing", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/smart-contracts/security.md", "source_location": "10. Resource exhaustion / fee griefing", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "If worst-case cost on attacker-shaped input exceeds network limits, legitimate users are denied service. Cap loops over user-controlled collections, per-iteration storage or events, and signature counts in __check_auth. Keep footprints small."}, {"id": "claude_skills_smart_contracts_security_check_auth_pitfalls", "label": "__check_auth Pitfalls", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/smart-contracts/security.md", "source_location": "11. Custom account (`__check_auth`) pitfalls", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Verify signature_payload itself. Enforce policy from auth_contexts, or a policy wallet is decorative. CAP-71 get_delegated_signers is unsanitized: verify each address is a registered delegate before delegate_auth."}, {"id": "claude_skills_smart_contracts_security_token_consumer_review", "label": "Token-Consumer Review", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".claude/skills/smart-contracts/security.md", "source_location": "Token-consumer review (AMMs, vaults, escrows, lenders)", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A contract that takes a token address must assume native XLM's SAC, a wrapped classic asset's SAC, or a custom contract. Decide allowlist versus permissionless. Store decimals at registration; never assume 7. Re-check the amount received when a token can deliver less than requested. Survive missing trustlines, AUTH_REQUIRED, frozen accounts, and clawback. transfer_from authorizes the spender, not from. Emit the standard token events."}, {"id": "claude_skills_smart_contracts_security_emergency_pause", "label": "Emergency Pause", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/smart-contracts/security.md", "source_location": "Contract", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Value-bearing contracts need pause controls and an incident runbook."}, {"id": "claude_skills_smart_contracts_security_scout", "label": "Scout", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/smart-contracts/security.md", "source_location": "Tooling", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "CoinFabrik cargo scout-audit: 20+ detectors, including missing overflow checks, unprotected WASM update, unrestricted transfers, unsafe unwrap, and unbounded-operation denial of service. SARIF output for CI."}, {"id": "claude_skills_smart_contracts_security_security_detectors_sdk", "label": "Security Detectors SDK", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/smart-contracts/security.md", "source_location": "Tooling", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "OpenZeppelin detectors such as auth_missing, unchecked_ft_transfer, and improper TTL extension, plus a framework for custom detectors."}, {"id": "claude_skills_smart_contracts_security_certora_sunbeam", "label": "Certora Sunbeam", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/smart-contracts/security.md", "source_location": "Tooling", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Formal verification with Rust macros (cvlr_assert!) over WASM bytecode."}, {"id": "claude_skills_smart_contracts_security_komet", "label": "Komet", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/smart-contracts/security.md", "source_location": "Tooling", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Runtime Verification property tests plus formal verification through KWasm semantics."}, {"id": "claude_skills_smart_contracts_security_openzeppelin_monitor", "label": "OpenZeppelin Monitor", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/smart-contracts/security.md", "source_location": "Tooling", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Self-hosted contract monitoring with Stellar support."}, {"id": "claude_skills_smart_contracts_security_sorobansecurity", "label": "sorobansecurity.com", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/smart-contracts/security.md", "source_location": "Tooling", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Searchable audit reports and a vulnerability database."}, {"id": "claude_skills_smart_contracts_security_audit_bank", "label": "Audit Bank", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/smart-contracts/security.md", "source_location": "Audits and bounties", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "SDF-subsidized audits for SCF-funded protocols. Partner firms include OtterSec, Veridise, Runtime Verification, CoinFabrik, Certora, Zellic, and Code4rena. Follow-up audits trigger at TVL milestones."}, {"id": "claude_skills_smart_contracts_security_immunefi_stellar", "label": "Immunefi Stellar", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/smart-contracts/security.md", "source_location": "Audits and bounties", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Up to $250K for core, SDK, and CLI vulnerabilities. A proof of concept is required, and only local forks are in scope."}, {"id": "claude_skills_smart_contracts_security_immunefi_openzeppelin", "label": "Immunefi OpenZeppelin on Stellar", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/smart-contracts/security.md", "source_location": "Audits and bounties", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Up to $25K for the audited OpenZeppelin contracts library on Stellar."}], "edges": [{"source": "claude_skills_smart_contracts_security_security_review", "target": "claude_skills_smart_contracts_skill_stellar_smart_contracts", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".claude/skills/smart-contracts/security.md", "source_location": "Security", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "claude_skills_smart_contracts_security_security_review", "target": "claude_skills_smart_contracts_development_development_patterns", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".claude/skills/smart-contracts/security.md", "source_location"